{"name":"Pink Ivory","hex":"#d6b3cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink ivory","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Hardwood of the African tree Phyllogeiton zeyheri (syn. Berchemia zeyheri)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink_ivory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pink ivory","blocks":[{"text":"Pink ivory, also called red ivory, purple ivory, unnini or umgoloti, is an African hardwood used to make a variety of products. The pink ivory tree grows predominantly in Zimbabwe, Mozambique, Northern Botswana and South Africa. The tree is protected and sustainably maintained in South Africa, only felled by very limited permit. The wood is extremely hard, with a density of 990 g/dm3."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Berchemia_zeyheri%2C_blare_en_blomknoppe%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/330px-Berchemia_zeyheri%2C_blare_en_blomknoppe%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_ivory","wikidata":"Q113881766"},{"title":"Ivory","blocks":[{"text":"Ivory is a hard, white material from the tusks and teeth of animals, that consists mainly of dentin, one of the physical structures of teeth and tusks. The chemical structure of the teeth and tusks of mammals is the same, regardless of the species of origin, but ivory contains structures of mineralized collagen. The trade in certain tusks and teeth other than elephant is well established and widespread; therefore, \"ivory\" can correctly be used to describe any mammalian teeth or tusks of commercial interest which are large enough to be carved or scrimshawed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Horn_Louvre_OA4069.jpg/330px-Horn_Louvre_OA4069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivory","wikidata":"Q82001"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"},{"title":"Ivory (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Ivory is an off-white color named after, and derived from, the material made from the tusks and teeth of certain animals, such as the elephant and the walrus. It has a very slight tint of yellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Decorated_ivory.JPG/330px-Decorated_ivory.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivory_(color)","wikidata":"Q1358981"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Red_Ivory_%28Phyllogeiton_zeyheri%29_5.jpg/500px-Red_Ivory_%28Phyllogeiton_zeyheri%29_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Red_Ivory_%28Phyllogeiton_zeyheri%29_5.jpg/1280px-Red_Ivory_%28Phyllogeiton_zeyheri%29_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Red_Ivory_%28Phyllogeiton_zeyheri%29_5.jpg/500px-Red_Ivory_%28Phyllogeiton_zeyheri%29_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Ivory_(Phyllogeiton_zeyheri)_5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Berchemia_zeyheri_1.jpg/120px-Berchemia_zeyheri_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://t